WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.620
13. Fighting for animals. A brief history.

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:11.830
The idea of animals having rights may seem new, but it's actually very old.

3
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:17.830
Teachers in ancient Greece debated with their students about eating meat and using animals for work.

4
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:25.830
In the Roman Empire, writers like Cicero, Virgil, and Plutarch argued that eating animals was cruel and unnecessary.

5
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.830
The first laws protecting animals were written in India around 240 B.C.

6
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:37.830
The modern Western animal rights movement began in the late 18th century and quickly gained support.

7
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:44.830
The Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, SPCA, was founded in England in 1824.

8
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:53.830
Elsewhere, the American Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, ASPCA, was founded in 1866.

9
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:57.830
These organizations worked to prevent animals suffering and pain.

10
00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.830
They protested against circuses and farms that treat their animals badly.

11
00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:07.830
They also fought against laboratories which performed painful or deadly experiments on animals.

12
00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:14.830
In 1966, the U.S. Congress passed the Animal Welfare Act to help protect animals and labs.

13
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:18.830
Since then, many other countries have passed similar laws.

14
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.830
The animal liberation movement began in the 1970s.

15
00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:28.830
It argued that animals should have the same rights as people and should not be used for meat, fur, or labor.

16
00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:36.830
Animal rights organizations promote vegetarianism and show people how painful fur making and factory farming really are.

17
00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:42.830
People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals, PETA, is one of the best known groups in this movement.

18
00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:49.830
Others, like the Animal Liberation Front, believe that helping animals is more important than following the law.

19
00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:51.830
Not everyone agrees with their methods.

20
00:01:51.830 --> 00:02:00.830
In recent years, organizations like Sea Shepherd, which focuses on protecting ocean life, have made animal rights a more wide-ranging issue.

21
00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.830
The fight goes on, but victories are being won.

22
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:12.830
Apes were given basic rights in New Zealand in 1999, and German law has recognized animal rights since 2002.
